e-methods#navigation","content":"| Method         | Purpose                             |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `go(position)` | Jump to a retained cursor position. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3044":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#navigation","content":"| Method                       | Purpose                        |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `canBack()` / `canForward()` | Check navigation availability. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3045":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#navigation","content":"| Method          | Purpose              |\n| --------------- | -------------------- |\n| `getPosition()` | Read current cursor. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3046":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#navigation","content":"| Method    | Purpose                                                   |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `reset()` | Restore the existing instance baseline through the owner. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3047":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#navigation","content":"Navigation publishes `go`. Manual pending work is archived as part of successful navigation. Controlled journals delegate patch application through `apply` and must not record that navigation again as a new external edit.","locale":"en"},"3048":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"| Method     | Purpose                                                 |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rebase()` | Keep current state and discard all past/future history. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"3049":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"| Method                                | Purpose                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `replaceStateWithoutHistory(updater)` | State-owning only: update state, clear history, establish a new baseline. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"3050":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"| Method                                 | Purpose                                                           |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pauseTracking()` / `resumeTracking()` | State-owning only: apply untracked updates around a new baseline. |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"3051":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#baseline-and-tracking","content":"Use these methods deliberately; they change what future undo and reset operations can reach.","locale":"en"},"3052":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-32","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#history-reads","content":"| Method         | Ownership and purpose        