,"page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","type":"page","content":"Release Checklist","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","locale":"en"},"3188":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"The project checklist for validating and publishing a Travels release.","locale":"en"},"3189":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Coordinated v3 binding release","locale":"en"},"3190":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"Update the release version locally:","locale":"en"},"3191":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"bump `package.json`","locale":"en"},"3192":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"update `CHANGELOG.md`, replacing `Unreleased` in the version heading with the release date","locale":"en"},"3193":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"Run local verification before tagging:","locale":"en"},"3194":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"Review README performance claims against `benchmarks/README.md`.","locale":"en"},"3195":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"Review persistence schema changes and migration notes.","locale":"en"},"3196":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"Confirm `docs/compatibility.md` still matches runtime support.","locale":"en"},"3197":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","content":"Commit the version and changelog changes to `main`.","locale":"en"},"3198":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"For a major release that changes the factory or restore boundary, publish in dependency order:","locale":"en"},"3199":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-11","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Finish every Travels gate in this checklist and publish `travels@3` from the exact tested artifact.","locale":"en"},"3200":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-12","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Install the published core in clean `use-travel` and `zustand-travel` checkouts. Raise their `mutative` peer and development ranges to the range Travels requires (`^2.0.0` for Travels 3), update their lockfiles to the published versions, and rerun each repository's types, tests, production build, and package smoke test.","locale":"en"},"3201":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-13","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Publish the binding majors only after those published-core runs pass.","locale":"en"},"3202":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-14","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"In a clean consumer, install all three published packages together with `mutative@2`, confirm the install reports no peer dependency conflict, and smoke test a new timeline plus an atomically restored timeline.","locale":"en"},"3203":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-15","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Local sibling links are useful candidate evidence, but they do not replace the published-package checks in steps 2 and 4. Do not tag a binding release that requires an unpublished core version.","locale":"en"},"3204":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-16","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Push `main`, then create and push a matching release tag:","locale":"en"},"3205":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-17","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"The tag must match the `package.json` version exactly, with a leading `v`.","locale":"en"},"3206":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-18","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"The release job picks the npm dist-tag itself: a version above the published `latest` becomes `latest`, a prerelease becomes `next`, and a maintenance release of an older major becomes `v<major>-latest` (for example `v2-latest`), so it never replaces the current major.","locale":"en"},"3207":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-19","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Confirm the tag-triggered release flow completed:","locale":"en"},"3208":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-20","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"`Release`","locale":"en"},"3209":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-21","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"`API Docs`, dispatched by `Release` with the release tag","locale":"en"},"3210":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-22","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"The documentation workflow publishes the release-tag build to `gh-pages`. Keep GitHub Pages configured to deploy from that branch at `/` (root). For an intentional website update outside a release, run `pnpm run deploy:doc:site` from the repository root instead of dispatching an older release tag.","locale":"en"},"3211":{"id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist-23","page_id":"/docs/resources/release-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/release-checklist#coordinated-v3-binding-release","content":"Smoke test the published package:","locale":"en"},"3212":{"id":"/docs/resources/security","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","type":"page","content":"Security Policy","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/security","locale":"en"},"3213":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security","content":"Supported versions and the responsible vulnerability reporting process.","locale":"en"},"3214":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/security#supported-versions","content":"Supported Versions","locale":"en"},"3215":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Reporting a Vulnerability","locale":"en"},"3216":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#supported-versions","content":"Security fixes are provided for the latest minor release of `travels`.","locale":"en"},"3217":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Please report security issues privately by opening a GitHub security advisory for this repository. Do not file public issues for vulnerabilities.","locale":"en"},"3218":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Include:","locale":"en"},"3219":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"affected version","locale":"en"},"3220":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"reproduction steps","locale":"en"},"3221":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"impact and affected APIs","locale":"en"},"3222":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"any known workaround","locale":"en"},"3223":{"id":"/docs/resources/security-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/security#reporting-a-vulnerability","content":"Maintainers will acknowledge valid reports as soon as practical, triage severity, and publish a patched release when needed.","locale":"en"},"3224":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing Strategy","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/testing","locale":"en"},"3225":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing","content":"Correctness, property-based, browser, mutation, and hot-path performance testing.","locale":"en"},"3226":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"Mutation smoke test","locale":"en"},"3227":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"Hot-path budgets","locale":"en"},"3228":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing","content":"Travels combines example-based, property-based, browser, package-consumer, coverage, and mutation smoke tests.","locale":"en"},"3229":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"Run:","locale":"en"},"3230":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"The smoke suite temporarily introduces a small set of high-value correctness regressions and verifies that focused tests fail. Every source file is restored in a `finally` block. The mutations cover backward replay ordering, controlled journal patch-pair validation, and mutable transaction rollback completeness.","locale":"en"},"3231":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#mutation-smoke-test","content":"This is intentionally a deterministic gate rather than a broad probabilistic mutation campaign. Add a mutation whenever a bug fix depends on a subtle operator, boundary, or rollback step that line coverage alone would not protect.","locale":"en"},"3232":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"Run:","locale":"en"},"3233":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"The matrix benchmark guards `setState` throughput and serialized history size. It does not cover undo/redo navigation or the controlled journal, and a change that made controlled navigation 53x slower and external commits 5.5x slower than the 2.1.0 line passed it unnoticed.","locale":"en"},"3234":{"id":"/docs/resources/testing-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/testing#hot-path-budgets","content":"`benchmarks/hot-path-check.js` measures per-operation cost for `setState`, navigation, transactions, and both controlled-journal paths, and fails the build when one exceeds its budget. The budgets are order-of-magnitude smoke limits, set far above the measured cost so shared CI runners do not flake; each scenario takes the best of three runs for the same reason. They are not percent-level drift detectors. Tighten a budget only alongside a measured improvement, and add a scenario whenever a new operation joins the timeline's hot path.","locale":"en"},"3235":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Resources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"3236":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","content":"Diagnose common update, navigation, persistence, mutable-mode, and integration problems.","locale":"en"},"3237":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"An update does not appear in history","locale":"en"},"3238":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"Undo or redo buttons stay stale","locale":"en"},"3239":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#instanceof-travels-fails-or-throws","content":"`instanceof Travels` fails or throws","locale":"en"},"3240":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"A restored snapshot throws","locale":"en"},"3241":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"JSON persistence loses values","locale":"en"},"3242":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-mutable-store-loses-or-unexpectedly-changes-its-root-reference","content":"A mutable store loses or unexpectedly changes its root reference","locale":"en"},"3243":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-transaction-did-not-roll-everything-back","content":"A transaction did not roll everything back","locale":"en"},"3244":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#observer-errors-or-reentrant-mutations","content":"Observer errors or reentrant mutations","locale":"en"},"3245":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Controlled journal history diverges from the owner","locale":"en"},"3246":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#the-website-needs-a-markdown-or-llm-version","content":"The website needs a Markdown or LLM version","locale":"en"},"3247":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#still-stuck","content":"Still stuck?","locale":"en"},"3248":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","content":"Use the sections below to isolate whether a problem belongs to state ownership, history recording, replay, persistence, or the UI binding. Stable error and warning codes are listed in Error Handling.","locale":"en"},"3249":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"Check these conditions in order:","locale":"en"},"3250":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Did the value actually change?** No-op patch groups create no entry and no event.","locale":"en"},"3251":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Is `autoArchive: false` enabled?** Pending updates need `archive()` or an operation that implicitly archives them.","locale":"en"},"3252":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Is tracking paused?** Resume it in a `finally` block.","locale":"en"},"3253":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Are you writing through Travels?** Direct assignments to `getState()`, a MobX/Vue store, or another owner are not recorded.","locale":"en"},"3254":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Are you using a controlled journal?** Call `recordPatches()` with the owner’s exact patch pair; journals intentionally omit `setState()`.","locale":"en"},"3255":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"**Did an updater throw or return a Promise?** Keep callbacks synchronous and await data before calling them.","locale":"en"},"3256":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#an-update-does-not-appear-in-history","content":"Use `getRevision()` to verify whether a committed event occurred and `subscribe()` to inspect the event type.","locale":"en"},"3257":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"State identity is not enough to invalidate controls. `archive()` and `rebase()` can change the timeline without replacing state.","locale":"en"},"3258":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"In React, subscribe with `useSyncExternalStore(travels.subscribe, travels.getRevision)`.","locale":"en"},"3259":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"In another store, mirror `getRevision()` or relevant controls after every committed event.","locale":"en"},"3260":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"Confirm the subscription was not disposed prematurely.","locale":"en"},"3261":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"Do not create a new timeline on every component render.","locale":"en"},"3262":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#undo-or-redo-buttons-stay-stale","content":"See Navigation and Controls.","locale":"en"},"3263":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#instanceof-travels-fails-or-throws","content":"The exported `Travels` value is a persistence namespace, not a constructor in Travels 3. Create instances with `createTravels()` and detect them with `isTravels(value)`. Controlled journals are not state-owning Travels instances and return `false` from that guard.","locale":"en"},"3264":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Parse storage before assuming its shape; `Travels.deserialize()` accepts JSON strings or parsed objects.","locale":"en"},"3265":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Use `validation: 'semantic'` for unverified input so invalid replay is detected at restore.","locale":"en"},"3266":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Match `strict` and `mark` through `replayOptions` when they were customized during recording.","locale":"en"},"3267":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Migrate older application and history shapes before validation.","locale":"en"},"3268":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Check `TravelsPersistenceError.code`, plus `entryIndex` and `direction` when present.","locale":"en"},"3269":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Supply a known-safe `fallback` for intentional startup recovery.","locale":"en"},"3270":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-restored-snapshot-throws","content":"Do not pass separate `history`, `initialPatches`, or `initialPosition` options in v3. Pass one complete snapshot to `restoreTravels()`.","locale":"en"},"3271":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"JSON does not preserve `undefined`, `bigint`, `NaN`, infinities, `-0`, prototypes, Map/Set, circular references, or shared object identity. Some values throw; others are silently converted or dropped.","locale":"en"},"3272":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"Run:","locale":"en"},"3273":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#json-persistence-loses-values","content":"Then inspect the reported path and normalize the value according to State Requirements. Remember that an incompatible value can remain in an old patch after leaving current state.","locale":"en"},"3274":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-mutable-store-loses-or-unexpectedly-changes-its-root-reference","content":"Check whether the operation replaced the root, used a primitive root, or navigated through a root-replacement patch. Prefer localized draft mutations. For restore, pass the observed object as `target` with `mutable: true`:","locale":"en"},"3275":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-mutable-store-loses-or-unexpectedly-changes-its-root-reference","content":"Do not combine mutable mode with `enableAutoFreeze`. Read the complete operation identity table.","locale":"en"},"3276":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-transaction-did-not-roll-everything-back","content":"Travels rolls back writes made through its own APIs. It cannot roll back direct mutable-store assignments, network requests, DOM changes, storage writes, or other external side effects.","locale":"en"},"3277":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#a-transaction-did-not-roll-everything-back","content":"Move every undoable state write into `setState()`, keep the callback synchronous, and manage external side effects after successful commit or with a separate compensation strategy. Framework observers attached directly to mutable state can also see provisional writes even though Travels observers cannot.","locale":"en"},"3278":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#observer-errors-or-reentrant-mutations","content":"Observers run after commit. They cannot veto or safely mutate the same transition. Schedule follow-up work in a later task and avoid cycles. Use `onObserverError` to isolate listener/devtools failures; an observer exception does not roll back the state that already committed.","locale":"en"},"3279":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Record the exact post-commit state and exact forward/inverse pair from the same transition.","locale":"en"},"3280":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Do not rerun the recipe inside Travels.","locale":"en"},"3281":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Do not record navigation triggered by `apply` as a new edit.","locale":"en"},"3282":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Make `apply` synchronous and return the state actually committed.","locale":"en"},"3283":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Handle root replacement explicitly when applying patches in place.","locale":"en"},"3284":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Preflight with `assertTravelHistoryEntryRecordable()` when the owner cannot roll back a published commit.","locale":"en"},"3285":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#controlled-journal-history-diverges-from-the-owner","content":"Travels validates patch structure but deliberately does not regenerate patches to prove the owner’s transition. That relationship belongs to the adapter.","locale":"en"},"3286":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#the-website-needs-a-markdown-or-llm-version","content":"Every documentation page exposes Markdown through the page’s copy/view controls. The site also exports `/llms.txt` and `/llms-full.txt` for documentation discovery and full-text consumption. These routes describe the documentation site; they do not change Travels runtime behavior.","locale":"en"},"3287":{"id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting-51","page_id":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/resources/troubleshooting#still-stuck","content":"Compare against a runnable Example, then open a GitHub issue with a minimal reproduction, the Travels and Mutative versions, runtime/browser details, stable error code, and the smallest state/patch payload that demonstrates the problem. Remove secrets and private user data first.","locale":"en"},"3288":{"id":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError","page_id":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError","type":"page","content":"TravelsError","breadcrumbs":["Travels","API 参考","类"],"tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError","locale":"zh"},"3289":{"id":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError-0","page_id":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError","content":"Travels 3.0.1. Travels 3 API reference for TravelsError.","locale":"zh"},"3290":{"id":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError-1","page_id":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh/docs/api-reference/classes/TravelsError#extends","content":"Extends","locale":"zh"},"329