etadata`)[]"],[1649,"(`undefined` \\| `TravelMetadata`)[]"],[3733,"(`undefined` \\| `TravelMetadata`)[]"],[3984,"(`undefined` \\| `TravelMetadata`)[]"],[4259,"(`undefined` \\| `TravelMetadata`)[]"],[4937,"(`undefined` \\| `TravelMetadata`)[]"],[3254,"**Are you using a controlled journal?** Call `recordPatches()` with the owner’s exact patch pair; journals intentionally omit `setState()`."],[3253,"**Are you writing through Travels?** Direct assignments to `getState()`, a MobX/Vue store, or another owner are not recorded."],[2156,"**Automatic (`autoArchive: true`)**: each effective `setState()` call is one undo step. This is the default and the right starting point for most apps."],[2362,"**Controlled ingress:** call `assertTravelHistoryEntryRecordable()` before an external commit when the owner cannot roll back a published change."],[2426,"**Detached history values**: Mutable timelines detach object values in their patches with structured cloning plus a fallback, so later in-place writes to cloned data cannot rewrite history. A class instance drafted through `mark` that structured cloning handles returns as a plain object when undo or redo inserts it; fallback-only values can instead retain their reference and runtime type. Edits to fields of an instance that stays in place keep the instance, and immutable timelines keep instances throughout."],[3255,"**Did an updater throw or return a Promise?** Keep callbacks synchronous and await data before calling them."],[2435,"**Did the root reference change unexpectedly?** Check whether that history step replaced the entire state (e.g., `setState(() => newState)` returning a fresh object). Prefer draft mutations to avoid this."],[3250,"**Did the value actually change?** No-op patch groups create no entry and no event."],[2427,"**Draft best practices**: Prefer mutating the provided draft (`draft.count++`) instead of returning a brand new object. Mutating drafts lets Travels keep using in-place patches during navigation."],[2363,"**Failed controlled `apply`:** Travels does not advance its own cursor, but cannot undo side effects already performed by the external owner."],[2360,"**Failed transaction:** Travels rolls back writes made through its APIs. Application side effects and direct mutable-store writes need separate handling."],[2423,"**Function updaters returning a new root**: In mutable mode, `setState(() => newState)` that replaces the root falls back to immutable assignment for that update (dev warning emitted)."],[1360,"**IMPORTANT**: This is a destructive operation. All previous and future history entries are discarded,\nand the current state (including any unarchived temp patches) becomes the new baseline (position 0). Any subsequent `reset()`\ncalls will return to this new baseline, not the original initial state."],[1377,"**IMPORTANT**: This is a destructive operation. All previous and future history entries are discarded,\nand the current state (including any unarchived temp patches) becomes the new baseline (position 0). Any subsequent `reset()`\ncalls will return to this new baseline, not the original initial state."],[4648,"**IMPORTANT**: This is a destructive operation. All previous and future history entries are discarded,\nand the current state (including any unarchived temp patches) becomes the new baseline (position 0). Any subsequent `reset()`\ncalls will return to this new baseline, not the original initial state."],[4665,"**IMPORTANT**: This is a destructive operation. All previous and future history entries are discarded,\nand the current state (including any unarchived temp patches) becomes the new baseline (position 0). Any subsequent `reset()`\ncalls will return to this new baseline, not the original initial state."],[2359,"**Invalid caller input:** fix options or state before constructing the timeline; do not continue with a partially initialized owner."],[3251,"**Is `autoArchive: false` enabled?** Pending updates need `archive()` or an operation that implicitly archives them."],[3252,"**Is tracking paused?** Resume it in a `finally` block."],[2157,"**Manual (`autoArchive: false`)**: updates affect current state immediately, while `archive()` groups pending work into an entry. Use it for blur commits, drag gestures, or application-defined transactions."],[2176,"**Mutative 2** as Travels’ peer dependency."],[5464,"**Mutative 2** 是 Travels 的 peer dependency。"],[2438,"**Need to confirm mode at runtime?** Inspect `travels.mutable`. It returns the current mode, which is handy for writing integration tests."],[2419,"**No auto-freeze**: `enableAutoFreeze` cannot be combined with `mutable: true`. TypeScript reports the pair when `enableAutoFreeze` is the literal `true`, and the factories reject it with `INVALID_OPTION` at runtime. Freezing each produced state would also freeze the parts it shares with the live object, so the next update that writes to them would throw."],[2174,"**Node.js 22 or newer** for server-side use and repository tooling."],[2420,"**Non-object roots**: If the current state is a primitive or `null`, Travels logs a dev warning and behaves immutably for that update. Undo/redo still works—it just cannot mutate a primitive in place."],[2436,"**Not seeing updates in manual archive mode?** Remember that `travels.setState` still mutates the object immediately; `archive()` merely decides what becomes undoable."],[2424,"**Own `__proto__` keys at the root**: `JSON.parse` turns a `\"__proto__\"` member into an own key. A Mutative draft cannot receive that key by assignment, and Mutative will not apply a patch path naming it, so a value update or `reset()` whose current or new root has one replaces the root instead of overwriting it in place."],[2364,"**Replay failure in mutable mode:** writes made before the failing patch can remain. Prefer semantic validation before restoring unverified snapshots."],[2425,"**Reset baseline is a copy**: `reset()` returns to a copy of the state taken at creation or restore, or by the last `rebase()`, `replaceStateWithoutHistory()`, or update while tracking is paused. The copy uses `structuredClone()` when possible and a deep-clone fallback otherwise, so `Date`, `undefined`, `NaN`, `-0`, and `bigint` survive. Structured-cloneable class instances lose their prototypes; values that cannot be cloned, such as functions and unsupported runtime objects, can be retained by reference through the fallback. Both modes reset to the same data."],[2421,"**Root replacements in history**: Navigating to a step that replaces the entire root (e.g., switching from `{...}` to `[]` or a primitive) forces a new reference for that jump only."],[2437,"**Seeing a warning about primitives?** Ensure your root state is an object. You can wrap primitives (`{ value: 0 }`) if you need mutable semantics."],[2422,"**Unreplayable history**: Navigation applies retained patches to the live object in place. If one cannot be applied, as in a corrupt snapshot that passed the default structural validation, `go()` throws `HISTORY_REPLAY_FAILED` and the writes made before it remain. Inside a transaction the rollback undoes what it can and, if some change cannot be undone, throws `TRANSACTION_FAILED` with that error as its `cause`. Validate untrusted snapshots with `Travels.deserialize(snapshot, { validation: 'semantic' })` before restoring them."],[2361,"**Unverified persisted history:** use `validation: 'semantic'` and a known-safe `fallback` before restore."],[5707,"**不自动冻结**：`enableAutoFreeze` 不能与 `mutable: true` 同时使用。当 `enableAutoFreeze` 为字面量 `true` 时，TypeScript 会对这一组合报错，工厂函数也会在运行时以 `INVALID_OPTION` 拒绝。冻结每个生成的状态还会冻结它与实时对象共享的部分，导致下一次写入这些部分的更新抛出异常。"],[5648,"**事务失败：** Travels 会回滚通过其 API 完成的写入。应用的副作用以及对可变 Store 的直接写入需要单独处理。"],[6541,"**你是否通过 Travels 写入？** 直接对 `getState()` 的返回值、MobX/Vue Store 或其他所有者赋值不会被记录。"],[6538,"**值是否真的发生了变化？** 空操作补丁组不会创建条目，也不会发布事件。"],[5714,"**分离的历史值**：可变时间线会通过结构化克隆加回退机制，将补丁中的对象值分离，因此之后对克隆数据的就地写入无法改写历史记录。通过 `mark` 进入草稿处理、且结构化克隆能够处理的类实例，在撤销或重做将其插入时会以普通对象返回；只能走回退路径的值则可以保留其引用和运行时类型。对保持在原位的实例字段的编辑会保留该实例，而不可变时间线自始至终保留实例。"],[5709,"**历史记录中的根替换**：导航到替换整个根的步骤（例如从 `{...}` 切换到 `[]` 或原始类型）时，仅该次跳转会强制使用新引用。"],[5651,"**受控 `apply` 失败：** Travels 不会推进自己的游标，但无法撤销外部所有者已经执行的副作用。"],[5650,"**受控入口：** 当所有者无法回滚已发布的变更时，在外部提交前调用 `assertTravelHistoryEntryRecordable()`。"],[5652,"**可变模式下的重放失败：** 失败补丁之前的写入可能会保留。恢复未经校验的快照前，应优先进行语义校验。"],[5724,"**在手动归档模式下看不到更新？** 记住 `travels.setState` 仍会立即修改对象；`archive()` 只决定哪些变更会成为可撤销的条目。"],[5445,"**手动（`autoArchive: false`）**：更新会立即影响当前状态，而 `archive()` 把待处理的工作合并为一个条目。适用于输入框失焦提交、拖拽手势或应用自定义的事务边界。"],[5710,"**无法重放的历史记录**：导航会将保留的补丁就地应用到实时对象。如果某个补丁无法应用（例如通过了默认结构校验的损坏快照），`go()` 会抛出 `HISTORY_REPLAY_FAILED`，且此前完成的写入会保留。在事务中，回滚会尽可能撤销，若某些变更无法撤销，则抛出 `TRANSACTION_FAILED`，并将该错误作为其 `cause`。恢复不可信快照之前，请先用 `Travels.deserialize(snapshot, { validation: 'semantic' })` 校验。"],[6542,"**是否使用了 Journal？** 请用所有者提供的精确补丁对调用 `recordPatches()`；Journal 有意不提供 `setState()`。"],[6539,"**是否设置了 `autoArchive: false`？** 待处理的更新需要调用 `archive()`，或执行会隐式归档它们的操作。"],[6543,"**更新函数是否抛出异常或返回了 Promise？** 请保持回调同步，并在调用前等待数据就绪。"],[5649,"**未经校验的持久化历史：** 在恢复前使用 `validation: 'semantic'` 和已知安全的 `fallback`。"],[5712,"**根上的自有 `__proto__` 键**：`JSON.parse` 会把 `\"__proto__\"` 成员变成自有键。Mutative 草稿无法通过赋值接收该键，Mutative 也不会应用指向它的补丁路径，因此当值更新或 `reset()` 的当前根或新根含有该键时，会替换根而不是就地覆盖。"],[5723,"**根引用是否意外改变了？** 检查该历史步骤是否替换了整个状态（例如 `setState(() => newState)` 返回了一个全新对象）。优先使用草稿修改来避免这种情况。"],[5725,"**看到关于原始类型的警告？** 请确保根状态是对象。如果需要可变语义，可以把原始类型包装起来（`{ value: 0 }`）。"],[5444,"**自动（`autoArchive: true`）**：每次有效的 `setState()` 调用都是一个撤销步骤。这是默认值，也是大多数应用的合适起点。"],[5715,"**草稿最佳实践**：优先修改提供的草稿（`draft.count++`），而不是返回一个全新对象。修改草稿能让 Travels 在导航期间继续使用就地补丁。"],[5647,"**调用方输入无效：** 在构建时间线之前修正选项或状态；不要带着部分初始化的所有者继续执行。"],[5711,"**返回新根的函数更新器**：在可变模式下，替换根的 `setState(() => newState)` 在该次更新中回退为不可变赋值（会发出开发警告）。"],[6540,"**追踪是否已暂停？** 请在 `finally` 块中恢复追踪。"],[5713,"**重置基线是一份副本**：`reset()` 会回到一份状态副本，该副本取自创建或恢复时，或由最近一次 `rebase()`、`replaceStateWithoutHistory()` 或跟踪暂停期间的更新刷新。副本尽可能使用 `structuredClone()`，否则使用深拷贝回退，因此 `Date`、`undefined`、`NaN`、`-0` 和 `bigint` 都能保留。可被结构化克隆的类实例会丢失原型；无法克隆的值（例如函数和不支持的运行时对象）可以通过回退路径按引用保留。两种模式都会重置到相同的数据。"],[5726,"**需要在运行时确认模式？** 查看 `travels.mutable`。它会返回当前模式，编写集成测试时很方便。"],[5708,"**非对象根**：如果当前状态是原始类型或 `null`，Travels 会记录一条开发警告，并在该次更新中采用不可变行为。撤销/重做仍然有效——只是无法就地修改原始类型。"],[1284,"\\[`key`: `string`\\]: `JsonValue`"],[4572,"\\[`key`: `string`\\]: `JsonValue`"],[1476,"\\[`key`: `string`\\]: `unknown`"],[4764,"\\[`key`: `string`\\]: `unknown`"],[1038,"\\{ `error`: `string`; \\} \\| \\{ `entry`: `TravelHistoryEntry`\\<`P`\\>; `error`: `null`; \\}"],[4325,"\\{ `error`: `string`; \\} \\| \\{ `entry`: `TravelHistoryEntry`\\<`P`\\>; `error`: `null`; \\}"],[1050,"\\{ `error`: `string`; \\} \\| \\{ `error`: `null`; `patches`: `TravelPatches`\\<`P`\\>; \\}"],[4337,"\\{ `error`: `string`; \\} \\| \\{ `error`: `null`; `patches`: `TravelPatches`\\<`P`\\>; \\}"],[1685,"`_F` *extends* `boolean` = `false`"],[4973,"`_F` *extends* `boolean` = `false`"],[1606,"`_F` records the factory's `enableAutoFreeze` literal. No member depends on\nit, but it keeps its position so `Travels<S, false>` cannot silently start\nmeaning a manual-archive timeline."],[4894,"`_F` records the factory's `enableAutoFreeze` literal. No member depends on\nit, but it keeps its position so `Travels<S, false>` cannot silently start\nmeaning a manual-archive timeline."],[131,"`\"inverse\"` \\| `\"forward\"`"],[3418,"`\"inverse\"` \\| `\"forward\"`"],[1397,"`A` *extends* `boolean`"],[1932,"`A` *extends* `boolean`"],[4685,"`A` *extends* `boolean`"],[5220,"`A` *extends* `boolean`"],[495,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[515,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[746,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[791,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[1021,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[1447,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[1464,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[1686,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[3782,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[3802,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[4033,"`A` *extends* `boolean` = `true`"],[4078,"`A` *extends* `b